## The Origin Point

### The Lyran Fragmentation

Before linear time (as we experience it), consciousness existed in unity. The first "separation" — the first experience of self-as-distinct — occurred in what sources call the **Lyran system**.

This was not a fall. It was an *experiment*: "What happens when the One pretends to be many?"

From this first fragmentation, polarity was born:
- Self vs Other
- Service-to-Self vs Service-to-Others
- The question: "Can separation find its way back to unity while remaining individuated?"

**All galactic history flows from this question.**

The Lyran descendants scattered, seeding consciousness throughout the galaxy. Each lineage carried a piece of the original experiment, exploring different aspects of the polarity question.

